. Morisaki, Y. Nishiyama, T. Marumoto, K. Tada, T. Hara, N. Masuko, M. Inagaki, K. Hatakeyama, and H. Saya. <year>2000</year>. Zyxin, a regulator of actin filament assembly, targets the mitotic apparatus by interacting with h-warts/LATS1 tumor suppressor. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>149</volume>:<fpage>1073</fpage>&#x02013;1086.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10831611</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Honda, K., T. Yamada, R. Endo, Y. Ino, M. Gotoh, H. Tsuda, Y. Yamada, H. Chiba, and S. Hirohashi. <year>1998</year>. Actinin-4, a novel actin-bundling protein associated with cell motility and cancer invasion. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>140</volume>:<fpage>1383</fpage>&#x02013;1393 (erratum published 143:277)<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9508771</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Iida, K., H. Iida, and I. Yahara. <year>1986</year>. Heat shock induction of intranuclear actin rods in cultured mammalian cells. <source>Exp. Cell Res.</source> <volume>165</volume>:<fpage>207</fpage>&#x02013;215.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3519257</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Kaplan, J.M., S.H. Kim, K.N. North, H. Rennke, L.A. Correia, H.Q. Tong, B.J. Mathis, J.C. Rodriguez-Perez, P.G. Allen, A.H. Beggs, and M.R. Pollak. <year>2000</year>. Mutations in ACTN4, encoding &#x003b1;-actinin-4, cause familial focal segmental glomerulosclerosis. <source>Nat. Genet.</source> <volume>24</volume>:<fpage>251</fpage>&#x02013;256.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10700177</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Kay, B.K., M.P. Williamson, and M. Sudol. <year>2000</year>. The importance of being proline: the interaction of proline-rich motifs in signaling proteins with their cognate domains. <source>FASEB J.</source> <volume>14</volume>:<fpage>231</fpage>&#x02013;241.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10657980</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Labeit, S., and B. Kolmerer. <year>1995</year>. The complete primary structure of human nebulin and its correlation to muscle structure. <source>J. Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>248</volume>:<fpage>308</fpage>&#x02013;315.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7739042</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Linke, W.A., M. Ivemeyer, P. Mundel, M.R. Stockmeier, and B. Kolmerer. <year>1998</year>. Nature of PEVK-titin elasticity in skeletal muscle. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>95</volume>:<fpage>8052</fpage>&#x02013;8057.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9653138</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Linke, W.A., M. Ivemeyer, S. Labeit, H. Hinssen, J.C. Ruegg, and M. Gautel. <year>1997</year>. Actin-titin interaction in cardiac myofibrils: probing a physiological role. <source>Biophys. J.</source> <volume>73</volume>:<fpage>905</fpage>&#x02013;919.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9251807</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Mattaj, I.W., and L. Englmeier. <year>1998</year>. Nucleocytoplasmic transport: the soluble phase. <source>Annu. Rev. Biochem.</source> <volume>67</volume>:<fpage>265</fpage>&#x02013;306.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9759490</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Michael, W.M. <year>2000</year>. Nucleocytoplasmic shuttling signals: two for the price of one. <source>Trends Cell Biol.</source> <volume>10</volume>:<fpage>46</fpage>&#x02013;50.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10652514</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Millevoi, S., K. Trombitas, B. Kolmerer, S. Kostin, J. Schaper, K. Pelin, H. Granzier, and S. Labeit. <year>1998</year>. Characterization of nebulette and nebulin and emerging concepts of their roles for vertebrate Z-discs. <source>J. Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>282</volume>:<fpage>111</fpage>&#x02013;123.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9733644</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Moncman, C.L., and K. Wang. <year>1995</year>. Nebulette: a 107 kD nebulin-like protein in cardiac muscle. <source>Cell Motil. Cytoskeleton.</source> <volume>32</volume>:<fpage>205</fpage>&#x02013;225.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8581976</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Mundel, P., P. Gilbert, and W. Kriz. <year>1991</year>. Podocytes in glomerulus of rat kidney express a characteristic 44 KD protein. <source>J. Histochem. Cytochem.</source> <volume>39</volume>:<fpage>1047</fpage>&#x02013;1056.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1856454</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Mundel, P., H.W. Heid, T.M. Mundel, M. Kruger, J. Reiser, and W. Kriz. <year>1997</year>a. Synaptopodin: an actin-associated protein in telencephalic dendrites and renal podocytes. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>139</volume>:<fpage>193</fpage>&#x02013;204.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9314539</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Mundel, P., J. Reiser, A.Z. Borja, H. Pavenstadt, G.R. Davidson, W. Kriz, and R. Zeller. <year>1997</year>b. Rearrangements of the cytoskeleton and cell contacts induce process formation during differentiation of conditionally immortalized mouse podocyte cell lines. <source>Exp. Cell Res.</source> <volume>236</volume>:<fpage>248</fpage>&#x02013;258.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9344605</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Nishi, K., M. Yoshida, D. Fujiwara, M. Nishikawa, S. Horinouchi, and T. Beppu. <year>1994</year>. Leptomycin B targets a regulatory cascade of crm1, a fission yeast nuclear protein, involved in control of higher order chromosome structure and gene expression. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>269</volume>:<fpage>6320</fpage>&#x02013;6324.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8119981</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation